repository-code: "https://github.com/kei-zan/dry-lab-modelling"
abstract: >-
  Computational design, audit and validation supporting an enkephalin-based analgesic
  strategy: a synthetic proenkephalin carrying seven tandem engineered opioid-peptide
  cassettes, released in vitro by reconstituted human prohormone convertases. The
  repository documents nine pre-registered design-build-test-learn cycles in which
  predictions and pass/fail gates were committed to version control before each test,
  including four methods that failed their own gates and are retained as negative results.
keywords:
  - synthetic biology
  - iGEM
  - enkephalin
  - proenkephalin
  - opioid receptor selectivity
  - free energy perturbation
  - molecular dynamics
  - pre-registration
